# T2 chain fixtures are compared BYTE-for-byte (MCP-Plugin-dotnet docs/chain-fixtures.md §F1), and the
# vendored chain_fixture.py and chain_feed.py are checked by sha256 against their canonical copies. A
# CRLF working copy (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) would break all of them, so pin them to LF.
/tests/chain-fixtures/** text eol=lf
/.github/scripts/chain_fixture.py text eol=lf
/.github/scripts/chain_feed.py text eol=lf
